        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fb6fd8d1-c643-5e4a-8532-652d3dda08f5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: North American Aviation\n- Products: T-6 Texan, P-51 Mustang, B-25 Mitchell, F-86 Sabre, X-15, XB-70, Apollo Command and Service Module, Saturn V second stage, Space Shuttle orbiter, B-1 Lancer\n- Organizations: United States Army Air Forces, United States Navy, Royal Air Force, British Commonwealth air forces\n- Topics: Aerospace manufacturing, military pilot training, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- North American Aviation was a major American aerospace manufacturer.\n- North American Aviation produced the T-6 Texan trainer, the P-51 Mustang fighter, the B-25 Mitchell bomber, the F-86 Sabre jet fighter, the X-15 rocket plane, the XB-70, the Apollo Command and Service Module, the second stage of the Saturn V rocket, the Space Shuttle orbiter, and the B-1 Lancer.\n- The North American Aviation T-6 Texan was an American single-engined advanced trainer aircraft.\n- During World War II, the T-6 Texan trained pilots for the United States Army Air Forces, the United States Navy, the Royal Air Force, and other British Commonwealth air forces.\n- The T-6 Texan remained in use into the 1970s.",
